{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>וְאָכַלְתָּ מִזִּבְחוֹ</b> ('and you eat of his sacrifice') — Are you so thinking that there is no punishment for eating it? For I bring upon you [accountability] as though you confess to its worship. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 34:15). And I say, according to the opinion of our Sages (Bava Kamma 71a, Ḥullin 40a), that this is a warning against one who eats offerings of idolatry, for they said that it is forbidden by Torah law, and we find no [source] for it other than this verse. And thus its meaning implies: 'lest you make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land and they stray after their gods, and they sacrifice to them always, and lest he call you and you eat of his sacrifice that he sacrifices to his gods, in straying after him, and lest you take of his daughters for your sons' (Exodus 34:16) — and behold, all of them are warnings flowing [as consequences] from the first negative [prohibition] that he stated: <b>פֶּן תִּכְרֹת בְּרִית</b> ('lest you make a covenant')."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:21:17.735917477Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}